🤔 What is a Function?
Think of Function as a Machine ⚙️

Coffee Machine:
→ You put coffee beans (INPUT)
→ Machine does its work
→ You get coffee (OUTPUT)

Function:
→ You give data (INPUT/PARAMETERS)
→ Function does its work
→ You get result (OUTPUT/RETURN)

# Without function - repetitive!
print("Connecting to web1...")
subprocess.run(['ssh', 'web1'])
print("Deploying to web1...")

print("Connecting to web2...")
subprocess.run(['ssh', 'web2'])
print("Deploying to web2...")

# With function - clean & reusable!
def deploy(server):
    print(f"Connecting to {server}...")
    subprocess.run(['ssh', server])
    print(f"Deploying to {server}...")

deploy('web1')
deploy('web2')
